1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,210
Bath or shower?
泡澡还是淋浴？

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:05,090
How do you prefer to keep yourself clean?
你更喜欢用哪种方式清洁身体？

3
00:00:05,090 --> 00:00:11,380
Whatever your daily ablutions, we know it’s important to have good personal hygiene.
无论你日常的洗浴方式是什么，我们都知道保持良好的个人卫生至关重要。

4
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:15,680
Nobody wants to smell, and nobody wants to catch your odour!
没人希望自己身上有异味，更没人愿意沾上别人的味儿！

5
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:23,820
A shower can bring you certain other benefits, but how often should we wash ourselves under a watery spray?
淋浴除了清洁，还能带来一些其他好处，但我们应该多久冲一次澡呢？

6
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:37,050
Although you might think taking a daily shower should be part of your cleaning ritual, there’s no hard and fast rule, although dermatologists agree that as a society, we shower too often.
你可能觉得每天淋浴是日常清洁的必不可少的一部分，但其实并没有硬性规定。

7
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:42,020
In fact, too much washing can deplete the vital oils in our skin.
不过皮肤科医生一致认为，在当今社会，我们洗澡的频率实在太高了。

8
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:44,980
It can waste water as well.
事实上，过度清洁会消耗皮肤中至关重要的油脂，同时还会造成水资源浪费。

9
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:55,300
However, if you have a fitness regime that causes you to sweat, a more regular sprinkle of water is recommended to stop you ponging!
但如果你有规律健身的习惯，运动后会大量出汗，那么就建议你更频繁地冲个澡，避免身上产生难闻的气味！

10
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:59,370
How often you shower is, of course, a personal choice.
多久洗一次澡当然是个人选择。

11
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:06,240
There’s nothing better than a hot, soapy scrub under the shower, and this doesn’t just have to be to clean yourself.
在花洒下用温热的肥皂水痛快地搓洗一番，这种感觉再好不过了，而且淋浴的目的也不只是为了清洁身体。

12
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:14,210
Some people enjoy a shower to help them relax, warm up or to soothe any aches and pains.
有些人喜欢通过淋浴来放松身心、让自己暖和起来，或是缓解身体的各种酸痛。

13
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:19,250
It’s also a good opportunity to wash your hair at the same time.
淋浴时也很适合顺便洗个头。

14
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:31,380
Again, though, experts say we shouldn’t shower too often because, like your skin, your hair contains essential oils that you don’t want to lose through excessive scrubbing.
不过专家同样提醒，洗头不宜过于频繁，因为和皮肤一样，头发中也含有不可或缺的油脂，过度清洗会导致这些油脂流失。

15
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:38,500
If the idea of a hot, steaming shower appeals, how about a freezing cold one instead?
如果热气腾腾的热水澡合你心意，那要不要试试冰爽的冷水澡呢？

16
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:49,620
This might be a necessity if your boiler has broken, but some people choose this option because it has many health benefits, some experts claim.
如果家里的热水器坏了，冷水澡就可能是不可避免的选择，但有专家称，有些人会主动选择冷水澡，因为它对健康大有裨益。

17
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:59,260
There is increasing evidence that braving an icy shower in the morning could keep illness at bay and may even help your brain stay sharp.
越来越多的证据表明，早上勇敢地冲个冷水澡，不仅能预防疾病，甚至还能帮助保持大脑思维敏捷。

18
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:11,100
A BBC podcast called Just One Thing with Michael Mosley, found the shock of being doused with cold water could have a positive impact on your body and brain.
迈克尔·莫斯利主持的BBC播客《一件小事》发现，身体被冷水浇透时的那种冲击感，会对身心产生积极影响。

19
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:23,760
The thought of a cold shower might not make you jump out of bed in the morning, but whatever the temperature, a splash of water will wake you up and make you feel and smell great!
想到早上要冲冷水澡，你可能对于起床这件事兴致缺缺，但无论水温冷热，冲个澡都能让你神清气爽，不仅体感舒适，身上还会香香的！
